the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base uses temporal includes these resources:
    temporal.

the templates are:
    *a person* was born on *a date*; undefined.
    *a person* can drive on *a date*.
    *a person* can vote on *a date*.
    *a person* claimed *an amount* on *a date*; undefined.
    the recent claims of *a person* on *a date* total *an amount*.

the knowledge base uses temporal includes:

a person can drive on a date if
    the person was born on a birth date
    and the age on the date of someone born on the birth date is a number N
    and N >= 16.

% The library's accessors are FUNCTIONS (§2.4), so the age can be written
% where it is compared instead of in a condition of its own.
a person can vote on a date if
    the person was born on a birth date
    and the age on the date of someone born on the birth date >= 18.

the recent claims of a person on a date total an amount T if
    the person was born on a birth date
    and T is the sum of each A such that
        the person claimed an amount A on a claim date
        and the claim date is within the last 3 months before the date.

scenario one is:
    ann was born on 2008-03-15.
    bob was born on 2010-01-01.
    ann claimed 100 on 2026-08-01.
    ann claimed 50 on 2026-05-01.
    before expects answers ["2026-02-28 is 3 calendar months before 2026-05-31"].
    drive expects answers ["ann can drive on 2026-09-13", "bob can drive on 2026-09-13"].
    vote expects answers ["ann can vote on 2026-09-13"].
    claims expects answers ["the recent claims of ann on 2026-09-13 total 100", "the recent claims of bob on 2026-09-13 total 0"].

query before is:
    which earlier date is 3 calendar months before 2026-05-31.

query drive is:
    which person can drive on 2026-09-13.

query vote is:
    which person can vote on 2026-09-13.

query claims is:
    the recent claims of which person on 2026-09-13 total which amount.

% Lengths of time written the ISO 8601 way, rhythms, a date without its year.
scenario iso_lengths is:
    periods expects answers ["2026-03-04 is the period PT72H after 2026-03-01"].
    months expects answers ["2027-02-28 is the period P1M after 2027-01-31"].
    earlier expects answers ["2025-12-31 is the period P12M before 2026-12-31"].
    third expects answers ["the occurrence 3 of every P1M after 2026-01-31 is 2026-04-30"].
    rhythm expects answers ["2027-03-01 is a date of every P1W from 2027-02-01 in the period from 2027-02-20 to 2027-03-05", "2027-02-22 is a date of every P1W from 2027-02-01 in the period from 2027-02-20 to 2027-03-05"].
    hours expects answers ["PT72H counts hours as whole days"].
    noyear expects answers ["the day 30 September in the year 2027 is 2027-09-30"].
    notiso expects answers [].

query periods is:
    which later date is the period "PT72H" after 2026-03-01.

query months is:
    which later date is the period "P1M" after 2027-01-31.

query earlier is:
    which earlier date is the period "P12M" before 2026-12-31.

query third is:
    the occurrence 3 of every "P1M" after 2026-01-31 is which date.

query rhythm is:
    which date is a date of every "P1W" from 2027-02-01 in the period from 2027-02-20 to 2027-03-05.

query hours is:
    "PT72H" counts hours as whole days.

query noyear is:
    the day "30 September" in the year 2027 is which date.

query notiso is:
    "P24H" is a length of time in the standard form.
